questions.question:
$$
\text{ Aqueous solution of } \mathrm{Na}_2 \mathrm{~S}_2 \mathrm{O}_3 \text{ on reaction with } \mathrm{Cl}_2 \text{ gives }
$$

questions.solution:
White phosphorus on reaction with $\mathrm{NaOH}$ gives $\mathrm{PH}_3$ as one of the product in disproportionation reaction

$\mathrm{P}_{4}+3  \mathrm{NaOH}+3  \mathrm{H}$}_{2} $\mathrm{O} \longrightarrow3 \mathrm{NaH}_{2}  \mathrm{PO}$}_{2}+ $\mathrm{PH}_{3}
$
